Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user requested moving the `home_repeater` field from the operators table (Stammdaten/Rufzeichen-Register) to the `exercise_repeaters` table, making it a per-exercise field displayed in BundMode next to the OP callsign input. This involved: (a) reverting the previous commit's Stammdaten/Auswertung changes across ~10 files, (b) implementing the new per-exercise approach with schema migration, API changes, socket sync, and BundMode UI. After initial implementation, the user iteratively refined the REP field: first changing it from text input to dropdown, then restricting to OE-Link repeaters only, then fixing the dropdown label to show site name + band instead of `short_name`.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - SQLite schema migrations using PRAGMA table_info checks
   - `exercise_repeaters` table: per-exercise repeater assignments with `operator_callsign` and new `home_repeater` columns
   - Socket.IO real-time sync pattern: emit event after API save, listen for broadcast in other clients
   - POST-then-PATCH pattern: try POST to create exercise_repeater row, catch conflict (409), then PATCH existing
   - `linkedRepeaters` = repeaters with `is_linked = 1` (OE-Link repeaters)
   - Deploy workflow: must `git push` before `./deploy-production.sh` because remote does `git pull`
   - Docker layer caching: COPY steps only invalidate when source files change on remote

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **`server/src/db/schema.ts`**
     - Added migration for `exercise_repeaters.home_repeater` column
     - Kept existing `operators.home_repeater` migration for deployed DB compatibility
     ```typescript
     // Migration: add home_repeater to exercise_repeaters (per-exercise repeater assignment)
     const erCols = db.prepare("PRAGMA table_info(exercise_repeaters)").all() as any[];
     if (!erCols.some((c: any) => c.name === 'home_repeater')) {
       db.exec("ALTER TABLE exercise_repeaters ADD COLUMN home_repeater TEXT DEFAULT NULL");
     }
     ```

   - **`server/src/routes/exercises.ts`**
     - POST `/:id/repeaters`: Added `home_repeater` to INSERT
     - PATCH `/:id/repeaters/:rid`: Changed from single-field update to dynamic partial updates supporting both `operator_callsign` and `home_repeater`
     ```typescript
     exercisesRouter.patch('/:id/repeaters/:rid', (req, res) => {
       const db = getDb();
       const updates: string[] = [];
       const params: any[] = [];
       if (req.body.operator_callsign !== undefined) { updates.push('operator_callsign = ?'); params.push(req.body.operator_callsign || null); }
       if (req.body.home_repeater !== undefined) { updates.push('home_repeater = ?'); params.push(req.body.home_repeater || null); }
       if (updates.length === 0) { res.status(400).json({ error: 'Keine Änderungen' }); return; }
       params.push(req.params.id, req.params.rid);
       db.prepare(`UPDATE exercise_repeaters SET ${updates.join(', ')} WHERE exercise_id = ? AND repeater_id = ?`).run(...params);
       res.json({ success: true });
     });
     ```
     - Removed `o.home_repeater` from stats participants query

   - **`server/src/services/socket.ts`**
     - Added `home_repeater_updated` socket event handler
     ```typescript
     socket.on('home_repeater_updated', (data) => {
       if (typeof data?.exercise_id !== 'string' || !UUID_RE.test(data.exercise_id)) return;
       socket.to(`exercise:${data.exercise_id}`).emit('home_repeater_updated', data);
     });
